  "notes": "Stadium boyband pop-rock with folk-stomp and 1980s-rock borrowings, windowed to the group's stated 2011—2016 run. The drums come straight off the entry: \"big reverbed kit, four-square kick with a stadium snare on 2&4, plus stomps, claps and a marching tom pattern on the folk-facing records; Bunetta's later records use a drier, more dynamic and subtle kit.\" So the kick anchors all four beats, the snare is hard under a large room tail with a wide clap offset for the stomp layer, and the perc lanes are `tom`, `tomLow` and `crash` at `downbeat` — the marching pattern — with the snare-roll ladder off. The wide `velocityVar` is the \"more dynamic and subtle\" half of that same sentence. No `bass808` block: \"no 808. Electric bass on roots and 5ths with an 8th-note drive\", so the cell shapes are root-fifth on a kick mirror. Harmony is \"bright majors with a IV—V—I anthem cadence\", carried at top weight. The arrangement block is where this entry is most specific and it is authored literally: the vocal arrangement, not the range, is the parameter — \"verse (traded lines) → pre-chorus (added voices) → chorus (all voices); a drums-out breakdown for a single soloist\" — which is the terraced structure with a deep `dropOutBeats`. \"Toplines are anthemic, ascending, and designed for crowd singing, with oh-oh wordless hooks\" is the arch contour and the raised `octaveJumpProb`; \"countermelody is a guitar riff or a stacked gang vocal\" is the two counter styles. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a medium-high rating because \"harmonic bands are lane-conventional\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register and `bpm.mode` 130 (the midpoint of the stated 120—140 anthem core) are INFERRED.",
